-- ================================================================
-- MINIMAL REPRODUCTION, NOW A REGRESSION FIXTURE — an operation's own type
-- variable did not thread through a call when the CALLER was generic in it.
--
-- Nothing here is about information flow, labels, specs, or dispatch. It is
-- twelve lines of ordinary generic code, and it is the root the guardians
-- example hit when a label-preserving operation could not be written in terms
-- of another one (WI-20260822-1FKR2; recorded as C10 in
-- examples/guardians/docs/design/measured.md).
--
--   anthill load docs/measurements/op-type-var-does-not-thread.anthill
--
-- FIXED 2026-08-22 (WI-20260822-1FKR2): the WHOLE FILE loads clean. The two
-- cases below are marked WAS REFUSED with the diagnostic each used to give, and
-- the ground case is kept as the control that pinned the failure on the
-- CALLER's polymorphism. `wi1fkr2_op_type_var_threads_test` loads this file and
-- asserts the clean load, so the record cannot drift from the loader.
-- ================================================================

-- ── case 1: a BARE type variable ─────────────────────────────────────────
-- The identity of the identity. `via_bare` promises exactly what `idv`
-- promises and its body is exactly `idv(x)`.
--
-- WAS REFUSED, with a diagnostic that asked to be reported:
--   type mismatch in via_bare.return (op-return): expected ?t, got ?t
--   (these render alike but are not the same type — the difference is in a
--    component this diagnostic does not print; please report it)
-- The two sides were two distinct FLEXIBLE variables — the caller's, and the
-- callee's own returned un-substituted — which `types_compatible` has no arm
-- for. Skolemizing the caller's makes them one `TermId` and one type.
namespace tv1
  operation idv(x: ?t) -> ?t
  operation via_bare(x: ?t) -> ?t = idv(x)
end

-- ── case 2: a variable NESTED in a sort application ──────────────────────
-- WAS REFUSED:
--   type mismatch in via.return (op-return): expected Box[T = ?t], got Box[T = b.T]
--
-- `b.T` was the tell, and it named the mechanism: the caller's own `?t` stayed
-- FLEXIBLE in the body, which is exactly what the unwritten-slot walk reads as
-- an omitted slot, so it overwrote the author's variable with the projection
-- "the T of the parameter b". The return kept `?t`, and the two stopped naming
-- one thing. Same root as case 1 — §5.4 quantifies a variable written in a
-- parameter type, and the body check was skolemizing only the `[A]` brackets
-- and the enclosing sort's parameters.
enum tv2.Box
  import anthill.prelude.{Int64}
  sort T = ?
  entity box(v: Int64)
end
namespace tv2
  import tv2.{Box}
  operation id(b: Box[?t]) -> Box[?t]
  operation via(b: Box[?t]) -> Box[?t] = id(b)
end

-- ── CONTROL: the same delegation with a GROUND caller ────────────────────
-- LOADED THEN AND LOADS NOW. This is what pinned the failures above as being
-- about the CALLER's polymorphism and not about delegation, arity, or the sort
-- itself; it stays as the row that would say so if a repair had merely stopped
-- checking returns.
enum tv3.Box
  import anthill.prelude.{Int64}
  sort T = ?
  entity box(v: Int64)
end
namespace tv3
  import anthill.prelude.{Int64}
  import tv3.{Box}
  operation id(b: Box[?t]) -> Box[?t]
  operation via_ground(b: Box[Int64]) -> Box[Int64] = id(b)
end
